## 6. Example VPC Architecture

Suppose we create the following network:

**VPC CIDR:** `10.0.0.0/16`

| Component | CIDR / Address | Purpose |
|---                  |---             |---                               |
| VPC                 | `10.0.0.0/16`  | Main virtual network             |
| Public Subnet A     | `10.0.1.0/24`  | Public web server                |
| Public Subnet B     | `10.0.2.0/24`  | High availability                |
| Private Subnet A    | `10.0.11.0/24` | Application server               |
| Private Subnet B    | `10.0.12.0/24` | Application server in another AZ |
| Database Subnet A   | `10.0.21.0/24` | Private database                 |
| Database Subnet B   | `10.0.22.0/24` | Database high availability       |

A production design may place subnets across at least two Availability Zones to improve resilience.

**Architecture flow:**

Internet → Internet Gateway → Public Web Tier → Private Application Tier → Private Database Tier

Private outbound IPv4 traffic may use a NAT Gateway when needed. Private AWS service access can use VPC endpoints where appropriate.

