## 9. Common VPC Problems and Solutions

| Problem                                   | Possible Solution                                                                    |
|---                                        |---                                                                                   |
| EC2 cannot access the internet            | Check the route table, gateway, public IP, security group, and NACL                  |
| SSH connection fails                      | Check the key pair, username, security group port 22, public IP, and routing         |
| Private instance cannot download packages | Check the NAT Gateway, its route to the IGW, and the private route table             |
| Two instances cannot communicate          | Check routes, security groups, NACLs, and IP addressing                              |
| VPC peering is not working                | Check the peering status, both route tables, security rules, and overlapping CIDRs   |
| S3 access fails from a private subnet     | Check the endpoint, route configuration, IAM permissions, and bucket policy          |
| Unexpected AWS networking charges         | Review NAT Gateway usage, data transfer, public IPv4 addresses, and unused resources |

